# DB MongoDB

**Enforced constraints:**

- MUST define schemas using Mongoose or Pydantic (even for schemaless MongoDB)
- MUST create indexes for common query patterns
- MUST choose embedding vs referencing appropriately (see guidelines below)
- MUST use aggregation pipelines for complex queries
- MUST avoid N+1 query patterns
- MUST validate schema changes don't break existing data
- MUST monitor index usage and query performance

**Embedding vs Referencing:**
- Embed when: one-to-few, data always accessed together, small subdocuments
- Reference when: one-to-many, many-to-many, large or independently accessed documents

See `instructions.md` for complete Mongoose and Motor examples, schema design patterns, indexing strategies, and aggregation pipeline examples.
